                <pb facs="0450" n="444" xml:id="pg444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/832: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-01-05T22:00:00+09:00">January 5, 1939—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 5—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. Our 6, January 1 [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>], 5 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>It has just been announced over the radio that Baron Hiranuma was this
                        evening installed as Prime Minister, and that Prince Konoye, who was
                        appointed President of the Privy Council as successor to Hiranuma, will join
                        the Cabinet as Minister without Portfolio. The former members of the
                        “inner-Cabinet” which was composed of Arita, Itagaki, Yonai, Ikeda and
                        Konoye remain in office with the exception of Ikeda who has resigned.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>A detailed report of the Cabinet changes will be telegraphed as soon as
                        official announcement is available.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
